* POKE - WRITE MEMORY BYTES

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* POKE - WRITE MEMORY BYTES

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    POKE hex-address hex-byte [hex-byte ...]

Writes bytes directly to the selected memory address. A quoted string form
is also supported by the resident implementation.

There is no file backup or memory protection implied. An incorrect address
can corrupt BYE, the command processor or buffered data. Use only for
deliberate private diagnostics on copied systems.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
